"\n<div class=\"brand-bar\"><img src=\"%%A0%%\" alt=\"Sophia Deutsch Akademie\" class=\"brand-logo\"><div class=\"brand-name\">Sophia Deutsch Akademie</div></div>\n<header class=\"lk-hd\"><div class=\"lk-topic\"><svg class=\"ic\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M13 3L5 13h6l-1 8 8-11h-6z\"></path></svg></div><div class=\"lk-kicker\">Lektion</div><div class=\"lk-big\">05</div><h1>현재형 동사변화와 명령형</h1><div class=\"lk-de\">Präsens und Imperativ</div><div class=\"lk-intro\">독일어 동사는 주어에 따라 끝이 바뀌어요.<br>동사원형에서 -en을 떼고 남은 어간에 인칭어미를 붙이면 현재형이 돼요 — lern-en → ich lern-e · du lern-st.<br>이 과에서는 규칙 동사, 발음 때문에 모양이 조금 바뀌는 동사, 모음이 바뀌는 동사, sein·haben·werden·wissen, 그리고 명령형까지 정리해요.<div class=\"x-goals\"><div class=\"x-goals-t\">이 과에서 익힐 것</div><div class=\"x-goal\">동사원형을 어간과 어미로 나눠요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">인칭어미 -e · -st · -t · -en · -t · -en을 붙여요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">어간이 -t·-d, -s·-ß·-z로 끝나는 동사의 변화를 지켜요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">du·er에서 모음이 바뀌는 동사를 구별해요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">sein·haben·werden·wissen의 현재형을 외워요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">du·ihr·Sie·wir에게 하는 명령형을 만들어요</div></div></div></header>\n<div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge review-badge\">복습</span><span class=\"sub-title\">2–4과 복습</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Kannst du ____ helfen? <span class=\"qh\">나를</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) ich</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) mir</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) mein</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) mich</button></div><div class=\"qe\">helfen + 3격 → mir (4과).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> Der Tisch ist neu. → ____ ist neu.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) Er</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Es</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Sie</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Ihn</button></div><div class=\"qe\">der Tisch → er (4과).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> Ich kaufe ____ Tisch. <span class=\"qh\">책상을 하나</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) eine</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) ein</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) einem</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) einen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">남성 4격 → einen (3과).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> das Auto의 복수형은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) die Autoer</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) die Autos</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) die Auton</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) die Autoe</button></div><div class=\"qe\">외래어 → -s (2과).</div></div></div>\n<section id=\"sec-A\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">A</span><h2>한국어로 먼저 보기</h2></div><p>한국어 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">주어<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">주어</span>문장에서 동작이나 상태의 주인이에요. 독일어 주어는 1격이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Der Hund schläft. → der Hund</span></span></span>가 바뀌어도 모양이 같아요 — 나는 배운다, 너는 배운다, 그는 배운다.<br>높임말이나 시제가 바뀔 때만 모양이 달라져요.<br>독일어 동사는 주어마다 끝이 바뀌어요 — ich lerne, du lernst, er lernt.<br>그래서 동사 끝만 봐도 주어가 누구인지 알 수 있어요.</p><div class=\"dgm\"><div class=\"dgm-cap\">한국어는 그대로, 독일어는 주어마다 끝이 달라요</div><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>주어</th><th>한국어</th><th>독일어</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>나는</td><td>배운다</td><td>ich lern<span class=\"x-e\">e</span></td></tr><tr><td>너는</td><td>배운다</td><td>du lern<span class=\"x-e\">st</span></td></tr><tr><td>그는</td><td>배운다</td><td>er lern<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td></tr><tr><td>우리는</td><td>배운다</td><td>wir lern<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td></tr><tr><td>너희는</td><td>배운다</td><td>ihr lern<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td></tr><tr><td>그들은</td><td>배운다</td><td>sie lern<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-B\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">B</span><h2>어간 + 인칭어미 — 규칙 동사</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">주어<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">주어</span>문장에서 동작이나 상태의 주인이에요. 독일어 주어는 1격이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Der Hund schläft. → der Hund</span></span></span>에 따라 끝이 바뀌어요. lernen에서 -en을 뗀 lern-에 ich는 -e, du는 -st, er는 -t, wir는 -en을 붙여요 — ich lern<strong>e</strong> · du lern<strong>st</strong>.</p></div></div><p><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사원형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사원형</span>사전에 실린 동사의 기본형이에요. 대부분 -en으로 끝나요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen · arbeiten · sammeln</span></span></span>은 대부분 -en으로 끝나요.<br>-en을 떼고 남은 부분이 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어간<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어간</span>동사원형에서 끝의 -en(-n)을 뗀 부분이에요. 여기에 인칭어미를 붙여요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen → lern-</span></span></span>이에요 — lernen → lern-, wohnen → wohn-, kaufen → kauf-.<br>어간에 주어에 맞는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">인칭어미<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">인칭어미</span>동사 어간 뒤에 붙어 주어가 누구인지 맞춰 주는 어미예요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lern-e · du lern-st · er lern-t</span></span></span>를 붙여요.</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-first\"><thead><tr><th>주어</th><th>어미</th><th>lernen<br>배우다</th><th>wohnen<br>살다</th><th>kaufen<br>사다</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ich</td><td>-e</td><td>lern<span class=\"x-e\">e</span></td><td>wohn<span class=\"x-e\">e</span></td><td>kauf<span class=\"x-e\">e</span></td></tr><tr><td>du</td><td>-st</td><td>lern<span class=\"x-e\">st</span></td><td>wohn<span class=\"x-e\">st</span></td><td>kauf<span class=\"x-e\">st</span></td></tr><tr><td>er · sie · es</td><td>-t</td><td>lern<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td><td>wohn<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td><td>kauf<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td></tr><tr><td>wir</td><td>-en</td><td>lern<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td><td>wohn<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td><td>kauf<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td></tr><tr><td>ihr</td><td>-t</td><td>lern<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td><td>wohn<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td><td>kauf<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td></tr><tr><td>sie · Sie</td><td>-en</td><td>lern<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td><td>wohn<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td><td>kauf<span class=\"x-e\">en</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"dgm\"><div class=\"dgm-cap\">여섯 칸, 실제 모양은 넷</div><div class=\"dgm-seq\"><div class=\"dgm-step\"><div class=\"dgm-num\">1</div><div class=\"dgm-step-b\"><div class=\"dgm-step-t\">wir = sie = Sie = 동사원형</div><div>wir lernen · sie lernen · Sie lernen</div></div></div><div class=\"dgm-step\"><div class=\"dgm-num\">2</div><div class=\"dgm-step-b\"><div class=\"dgm-step-t\">er = ihr</div><div>er lernt · ihr lernt — 둘 다 -t</div></div></div><div class=\"dgm-step\"><div class=\"dgm-num\">3</div><div class=\"dgm-step-b\"><div class=\"dgm-step-t\">du만 -st</div><div>du lernst</div></div></div><div class=\"dgm-step\"><div class=\"dgm-num\">4</div><div class=\"dgm-step-b\"><div class=\"dgm-step-t\">ich만 -e</div><div>ich lerne</div></div></div></div></div><p>같은 방식으로 변하는 동사 — machen 하다 · spielen 놀다 · kommen 오다 · gehen 가다 · trinken 마시다 · schreiben 쓰다 · hören 듣다 · fragen 묻다 · brauchen 필요하다 · suchen 찾다 · bleiben 머물다 · studieren 대학에서 공부하다.</p><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">규칙 동사</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Wir ____ in Seoul. <span class=\"qh\">wohnen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) wohnst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) wohnt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) wohnen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) wohne</button></div><div class=\"qe\">wir → 원형과 같은 -en.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> Du ____ gut Deutsch. <span class=\"qh\">lernen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) lerne</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) lernen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) lernt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) lernst</button></div><div class=\"qe\">du → -st.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> Ihr ____ Fußball. <span class=\"qh\">spielen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) spielt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) spielst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) spielen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) spiele</button></div><div class=\"qe\">ihr → -t (er와 같아요).</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> Er ____ Kaffee. <span class=\"qh\">trinken</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) trinkst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) trinke</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) trinkt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) trinken</button></div><div class=\"qe\">er → -t.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> Ich ____ aus Korea. <span class=\"qh\">kommen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) komme</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) kommt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) kommst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) kommen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">ich → -e.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">6.</strong> Sie(존칭) ____ Musik. <span class=\"qh\">hören</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) höre</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) hörst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) hört</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) hören</button></div><div class=\"qe\">Sie → 원형과 같은 -en.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-C\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">C</span><h2>발음 때문에 모양이 바뀌는 동사</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">발음하기 어려운 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 모양을 조금 바꿔요. arbeiten은 du arbeit<strong>est</strong>처럼 e를 하나 넣어요.</p></div></div><p><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어미<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어미</span>단어 끝에 붙어 문법 정보를 나타내는 부분이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lern-e · gut-er · Kind-er</span></span></span>를 그대로 붙이면 발음이 어려운 동사는 모양을 조금 바꿔요. 변화 원리는 규칙 동사와 같아요.</p><h3>① 어간이 -t · -d로 끝나면 → -e-를 넣어요</h3><p>du·er·ihr의 어미 앞에 -e-를 넣어요. arbeit-t는 발음이 안 되니까 arbeit-e-t가 돼요.<br>-chn·-ffn·-gn·-tm으로 끝나는 동사도 같아요 — rechnen 계산하다, öffnen 열다, regnen 비가 오다, atmen 숨 쉬다.</p><h3>② 어간이 -s · -ß · -z · -x로 끝나면 → du에 -t만</h3><p>du의 -st에서 s가 겹치니까 -t만 붙여요. 그래서 du와 er의 모양이 같아져요.</p><h3>③ -eln · -ern 동사 → 원형이 -n으로 끝나요</h3><p>wir·sie·Sie의 어미가 -n이에요. -eln 동사는 ich에서 e가 빠져요(ich sammle).</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-first t-wide\"><thead><tr><th>주어</th><th>arbeiten<br>일하다</th><th>finden<br>찾다</th><th>reisen<br>여행하다</th><th>heißen<br>이름이 ~⁠이다</th><th>sammeln<br>모으다</th><th>wandern<br>등산하다</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ich</td><td>arbeite</td><td>finde</td><td>reise</td><td>heiße</td><td>samm<span class=\"x-e\">le</span></td><td>wandere</td></tr><tr><td>du</td><td>arbeit<span class=\"x-e\">est</span></td><td>find<span class=\"x-e\">est</span></td><td>reis<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td><td>heiß<span class=\"x-e\">t</span></td><td>sammelst</td><td>wanderst</td></tr><tr><td>er · sie · es</td><td>arbeit<span class=\"x-e\">et</span></td><td>find<span class=\"x-e\">et</span></td><td>reist</td><td>heißt</td><td>sammelt</td><td>wandert</td></tr><tr><td>wir</td><td>arbeiten</td><td>finden</td><td>reisen</td><td>heißen</td><td>sammel<span class=\"x-e\">n</span></td><td>wander<span class=\"x-e\">n</span></td></tr><tr><td>ihr</td><td>arbeit<span class=\"x-e\">et</span></td><td>find<span class=\"x-e\">et</span></td><td>reist</td><td>heißt</td><td>sammelt</td><td>wandert</td></tr><tr><td>sie · Sie</td><td>arbeiten</td><td>finden</td><td>reisen</td><td>heißen</td><td>sammel<span class=\"x-e\">n</span></td><td>wander<span class=\"x-e\">n</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">발음 때문에 바뀌는 동사</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Er ____ in Berlin. <span class=\"qh\">arbeiten</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) arbeiten</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) arbeit</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) arbeitet</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) arbeitt</button></div><div class=\"qe\">어간 -t → -e-를 넣어요.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> Wie ____ du? <span class=\"qh\">heißen · 이름이 뭐야?</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) heißst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) heißt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) heiße</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) heißest</button></div><div class=\"qe\">어간 -ß → du에 -t만.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> Du ____ den Schlüssel nicht. <span class=\"qh\">finden</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) findet</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) findst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) findest</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) finden</button></div><div class=\"qe\">어간 -d → du findest.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> Ich ____ Briefmarken. <span class=\"qh\">sammeln</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) sammele</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) sammle</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) sammeln</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) sammel</button></div><div class=\"qe\">-eln 동사는 ich에서 e가 빠져요.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> Wir ____ gern. <span class=\"qh\">wandern</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) wandert</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) wanderst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) wanderen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) wandern</button></div><div class=\"qe\">-ern 동사 → wir는 원형 그대로 wandern.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">6.</strong> Du ____ viel. <span class=\"qh\">tanzen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) tanzt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) tanzst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) tanze</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) tanzest</button></div><div class=\"qe\">어간 -z → du에 -t만.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">7.</strong> Es ____. <span class=\"qh\">regnen · 비가 와요</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) regnen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) regnt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) regnet</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) regen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">어간 -gn → -e-를 넣어 regnet.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-D\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">D</span><h2>모음이 바뀌는 동사</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">몇몇 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 du와 er에서만 모음이 바뀌어요 — fahren → du f<strong>ä</strong>hrst · sprechen → er spr<strong>i</strong>cht.</p></div></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" alt=\"Er fährt Auto. 그는 운전해요. (a → ä) / Er spricht Deutsch. 그는 독일어를 해요. (e → i)\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption class=\"ph-pair\"><div><span class=\"ph-de\">Er <strong>fährt</strong> Auto.</span><span class=\"ph-ko\">그는 운전해요. a → ä</span></div><div><span class=\"ph-de\">Er <strong>spricht</strong> Deutsch.</span><span class=\"ph-ko\">그는 독일어를 해요. e → i</span></div></figcaption></figure><p>자주 쓰는 동사 가운데 du와 er·sie·es에서만 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어간<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어간</span>동사원형에서 끝의 -en(-n)을 뗀 부분이에요. 여기에 인칭어미를 붙여요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen → lern-</span></span></span>의 모음이 바뀌는 동사가 있어요.<br>ich·wir·ihr·sie는 바뀌지 않아요. <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어미<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어미</span>단어 끝에 붙어 문법 정보를 나타내는 부분이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lern-e · gut-er · Kind-er</span></span></span>는 규칙 동사와 같아요.</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-first\"><thead><tr><th>주어</th><th>sprechen<br>말하다 (e→i)</th><th>lesen<br>읽다 (e→ie)</th><th>fahren<br>타고 가다 (a→ä)</th><th>laufen<br>달리다 (au→äu)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ich</td><td>spreche</td><td>lese</td><td>fahre</td><td>laufe</td></tr><tr><td>du</td><td>spr<span class=\"x-e\">i</span>chst</td><td>l<span class=\"x-e\">ie</span>st</td><td>f<span class=\"x-e\">ä</span>hrst</td><td>l<span class=\"x-e\">äu</span>fst</td></tr><tr><td>er · sie · es</td><td>spr<span class=\"x-e\">i</span>cht</td><td>l<span class=\"x-e\">ie</span>st</td><td>f<span class=\"x-e\">ä</span>hrt</td><td>l<span class=\"x-e\">äu</span>ft</td></tr><tr><td>wir</td><td>sprechen</td><td>lesen</td><td>fahren</td><td>laufen</td></tr><tr><td>ihr</td><td>sprecht</td><td>lest</td><td>fahrt</td><td>lauft</td></tr><tr><td>sie · Sie</td><td>sprechen</td><td>lesen</td><td>fahren</td><td>laufen</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>자주 쓰는 모음 변화 동사</h3><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left\"><thead><tr><th>변화</th><th>동사</th><th>du · er</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>e → i</td><td>sprechen 말하다 · helfen 돕다 · geben 주다 · essen 먹다 · treffen 만나다 · vergessen 잊다</td><td>sprichst · spricht / hilfst · hilft / gibst · gibt / isst · isst / triffst · trifft / vergisst · vergisst</td></tr><tr><td>e → ie</td><td>lesen 읽다 · sehen 보다 · empfehlen 추천하다</td><td>liest · liest / siehst · sieht / empfiehlst · empfiehlt</td></tr><tr><td>a → ä</td><td>fahren 타고 가다 · schlafen 자다 · tragen 나르다·입다 · waschen 씻다 · fallen 떨어지다</td><td>fährst · fährt / schläfst · schläft / trägst · trägt / wäschst · wäscht / fällst · fällt</td></tr><tr><td>au → äu</td><td>laufen 달리다</td><td>läufst · läuft</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout callout-warn\"><span class=\"co-badge co-warn\">모양이 더 많이 바뀌는 동사</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">nehmen 잡다 → du nimmst · er nimmt (h가 빠지고 m이 둘)<br>halten 붙잡다·멈추다 → du hältst · er hält (어미 -et 없음)<br>lassen 두다·시키다 → du lässt · er lässt<br>treten 밟다 → du trittst · er tritt<br>이 동사들은 du·er 형태를 통째로 외워요.</p></div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">모음 변화 동사</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Er ____ Deutsch und Englisch. <span class=\"qh\">sprechen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) sprecht</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) sprichst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) sprecht</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) spricht</button></div><div class=\"qe\">e → i, er → spricht.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> Du ____ zu schnell. <span class=\"qh\">fahren</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) fährst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) fährt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) fahrst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) fahrt</button></div><div class=\"qe\">a → ä, du → fährst.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> ____ du gern Bücher? <span class=\"qh\">lesen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Lies</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) Liest</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Lest</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Lesst</button></div><div class=\"qe\">e → ie, 어간 -s → du liest.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> Ich ____ den Bus. <span class=\"qh\">nehmen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) nimme</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) nehm</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) nehme</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) nimmst</button></div><div class=\"qe\">ich는 모음이 바뀌지 않아요.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> Er ____ ein Taxi. <span class=\"qh\">nehmen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) nehmt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) nimmst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) nehmet</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) nimmt</button></div><div class=\"qe\">nehmen → er nimmt.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">6.</strong> Ihr ____ zu viel. <span class=\"qh\">essen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) isst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) esst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) ist</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) essen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">ihr는 모음이 바뀌지 않아요 → esst.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">7.</strong> Das Kind ____ lange. <span class=\"qh\">schlafen</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) schläft</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) schläfst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) schlafen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) schlaft</button></div><div class=\"qe\">a → ä, er/es → schläft.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">8.</strong> Der Bus ____ hier. <span class=\"qh\">halten · 버스가 여기 서요</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) haltet</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) hält</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) halt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) hältet</button></div><div class=\"qe\">halten → er hält (어미 -et 없음).</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-E\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">E</span><h2>sein · haben · werden · wissen</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">가장 자주 쓰는 네 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>는 규칙을 따르지 않으니 통째로 외워요 — ich <strong>bin</strong> · du <strong>hast</strong> · er <strong>wird</strong> · ich <strong>weiß</strong>.</p></div></div><p>가장 자주 쓰는 동사들은 규칙에서 크게 벗어나요. 표를 통째로 외워요.</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-first\"><thead><tr><th>주어</th><th>sein<br>~⁠이다·있다</th><th>haben<br>가지다</th><th>werden<br>되다</th><th>wissen<br>알다</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ich</td><td><strong>bin</strong></td><td>habe</td><td>werde</td><td><strong>weiß</strong></td></tr><tr><td>du</td><td><strong>bist</strong></td><td><strong>hast</strong></td><td><strong>wirst</strong></td><td><strong>weißt</strong></td></tr><tr><td>er · sie · es</td><td><strong>ist</strong></td><td><strong>hat</strong></td><td><strong>wird</strong></td><td><strong>weiß</strong></td></tr><tr><td>wir</td><td><strong>sind</strong></td><td>haben</td><td>werden</td><td>wissen</td></tr><tr><td>ihr</td><td><strong>seid</strong></td><td>habt</td><td>werdet</td><td>wisst</td></tr><tr><td>sie · Sie</td><td><strong>sind</strong></td><td>haben</td><td>werden</td><td>wissen</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"exl\"><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich <strong>bin</strong> müde.</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">저 피곤해요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\"><strong>Hast</strong> du Zeit?</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">너 시간 있어?</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Es <strong>wird</strong> kalt.</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">추워지고 있어요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich <strong>weiß</strong> es nicht.</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">그건 잘 모르겠어요.</span></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-key\"><span class=\"co-badge \">wissen과 kennen</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">wissen은 '사실·정보를 알다', kennen은 '사람·장소·작품을 직접 알다'예요.<br>Ich <strong>weiß</strong>, wo er wohnt. 그가 어디 사는지 알아요. · Ich <strong>kenne</strong> ihn. 나는 그를 알아요.<br>wissen은 ich와 er의 모양이 같고 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어미<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어미</span>단어 끝에 붙어 문법 정보를 나타내는 부분이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lern-e · gut-er · Kind-er</span></span></span>가 없어요 — ich weiß · er weiß.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">werden의 세 가지 쓰임</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">werden은 '되다'라는 뜻 외에 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">미래형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">미래형</span>werden + 원형으로 앞으로의 일을 말하는 형태예요. 독일어는 미래도 현재형으로 자주 말해요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich werde morgen kommen.</span></span></span>(26과)과 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">수동태<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">수동태</span>행동을 하는 사람보다 행동을 받는 대상을 주어로 세우는 문장이에요. werden + 과거분사.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Das Haus wird gebaut.</span></span></span>(31과)를 만드는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">보조 동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">보조 동사</span>완료형·미래형·수동태를 만들 때 두 번째 자리에서 인칭과 시제만 맡는 haben·sein·werden이에요. 화법조동사와는 다른 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich habe gelernt. → habe</span></span></span>로도 쓰여요.<br>지금은 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">현재형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">현재형</span>지금의 일, 습관, 가까운 미래를 말할 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich lerne Deutsch.</span></span></span> 표만 외워 두면 돼요.</p></div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">sein · haben · werden · wissen</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> Wir ____ Studenten.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) sein</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) seid</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) sind</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) ist</button></div><div class=\"qe\">sein: wir sind.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> ____ ihr Hunger?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) Habt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Haben</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Hat</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Hast</button></div><div class=\"qe\">haben: ihr habt.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> Er ____ Arzt. <span class=\"qh\">그는 의사가 돼요</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) werd</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) wird</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) werdet</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) wirst</button></div><div class=\"qe\">werden: er wird.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> ____ du, wo der Bahnhof ist?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) Weißt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Weiß</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Kennst</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Wisst</button></div><div class=\"qe\">정보를 아는지 묻는 말 → wissen, du weißt.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> Ich ____ den Mann nicht. <span class=\"qh\">그 남자를 몰라요</span></div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) weiß</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) kennt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) wisse</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) kenne</button></div><div class=\"qe\">사람을 알다 → kennen.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">6.</strong> Du ____ sehr nett.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) ist</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) bin</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) seid</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) bist</button></div><div class=\"qe\">sein: du bist.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-F\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">F</span><h2>현재형의 쓰임</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">현재형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">현재형</span>지금의 일, 습관, 가까운 미래를 말할 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich lerne Deutsch.</span></span></span>은 지금 일뿐 아니라 습관과 가까운 미래에도 써요 — Ich <strong>lerne</strong> jeden Tag Deutsch. 매일 독일어를 공부해요.</p></div></div><p>독일어 현재형은 한국어 현재형보다 쓰임이 넓어요.</p><div class=\"dgm-seq\"><div class=\"dgm-step\"><div class=\"dgm-num\">1</div><div class=\"dgm-step-b\"><div class=\"dgm-step-t\">지금 하는 일</div><div>Ich lese gerade ein Buch. — 지금 책을 읽고 있어요. (영어 -ing 형태가 따로 없어요)</div></div></div><div class=\"dgm-step\"><div class=\"dgm-num\">2</div><div class=\"dgm-step-b\"><div class=\"dgm-step-t\">습관·늘 그런 일</div><div>Ich trinke morgens Kaffee. — 아침마다 커피를 마셔요.</div></div></div><div class=\"dgm-step\"><div class=\"dgm-num\">3</div><div class=\"dgm-step-b\"><div class=\"dgm-step-t\">가까운 미래 (시간 표현과 함께)</div><div>Morgen fahre ich nach Busan. — 내일 부산에 가요.</div></div></div><div class=\"dgm-step\"><div class=\"dgm-num\">4</div><div class=\"dgm-step-b\"><div class=\"dgm-step-t\">과거에 시작해 지금도 계속되는 일</div><div>Ich wohne seit zwei Jahren in Seoul. — 2년째 서울에 살고 있어요.</div></div></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">seit + 현재형</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">'2년째 살고 있다'를 독일어는 현재형으로 말해요. 아직 끝나지 않은 일이기 때문이에요.<br>✕ Ich habe seit zwei Jahren in Seoul gewohnt. → ✓ Ich wohne seit zwei Jahren in Seoul.</p></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-G\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">G</span><h2>명령형 — 부탁하고 지시하기</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-easy\"><span class=\"co-badge co-easy\">쉽게 말하면</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">명령형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">명령형</span>부탁·지시·권유를 할 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요. 동사가 문장 맨 앞에 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Komm! · Kommt! · Kommen Sie!</span></span></span>은 부탁하거나 지시할 때 써요. <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">동사</span>동작이나 상태를 나타내는 말이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen 배우다 · sein ~이다</span></span></span>가 맨 앞에 와요 — <strong>Komm</strong>! 와! · <strong>Kommen Sie</strong> bitte! 오세요!</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-scroll\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 600 266\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"명령형은 현재형에서 만들어요 — du와 -st를 빼고, ihr를 빼고, Sie는 자리를 바꿔요\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><defs><marker id=\"imperative-ink\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mki\"/></marker><marker id=\"imperative-acc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mka\"/></marker><marker id=\"imperative-ok\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mko\"/></marker><marker id=\"imperative-no\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mkn\"/></marker><marker id=\"imperative-w\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8.6\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" class=\"f-mkw\"/></marker></defs><text x=\"140.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-m\" font-weight=\"700\">현재형</text><text x=\"388.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-a\" font-weight=\"700\">명령형</text><text x=\"16.0\" y=\"78.0\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">du</text><rect x=\"64.0\" y=\"52.0\" width=\"41.4\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-boxn\"/><text x=\"84.7\" y=\"78.5\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-not\" font-weight=\"700\">du</text><rect x=\"111.4\" y=\"52.0\" width=\"91.7\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-box\"/><text x=\"157.2\" y=\"78.5\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">komm<tspan font-weight=\"700\" class=\"f-not\">st</tspan></text><line x1=\"71.0\" y1=\"84.0\" x2=\"98.4\" y2=\"60.0\" style=\"stroke:var(--no);stroke-width:2.5\"/><line x1=\"215.1\" y1=\"72.0\" x2=\"294.0\" y2=\"72.0\" class=\"f-la\" marker-end=\"url(#imperative-acc)\"/><rect x=\"306.0\" y=\"52.0\" width=\"82.6\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-boxa\"/><text x=\"347.3\" y=\"78.5\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-a\" font-weight=\"700\">Komm!</text><text x=\"402.6\" y=\"77.0\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" class=\"f-m\">du와 -st를 빼요</text><text x=\"16.0\" y=\"148.0\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">ihr</text><rect x=\"64.0\" y=\"122.0\" width=\"44.4\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-boxn\"/><text x=\"86.2\" y=\"148.5\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-not\" font-weight=\"700\">ihr</text><rect x=\"114.4\" y=\"122.0\" width=\"81.1\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-box\"/><text x=\"155.0\" y=\"148.5\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">kommt</text><line x1=\"71.0\" y1=\"154.0\" x2=\"101.4\" y2=\"130.0\" style=\"stroke:var(--no);stroke-width:2.5\"/><line x1=\"207.5\" y1=\"142.0\" x2=\"294.0\" y2=\"142.0\" class=\"f-la\" marker-end=\"url(#imperative-acc)\"/><rect x=\"306.0\" y=\"122.0\" width=\"89.5\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-boxa\"/><text x=\"350.7\" y=\"148.5\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-a\" font-weight=\"700\">Kommt!</text><text x=\"409.5\" y=\"147.0\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" class=\"f-m\">ihr만 빼요</text><text x=\"16.0\" y=\"218.0\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"start\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">Sie</text><rect x=\"64.0\" y=\"192.0\" width=\"50.5\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-box\"/><text x=\"89.3\" y=\"218.5\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">Sie</text><rect x=\"120.5\" y=\"192.0\" width=\"95.6\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-box\"/><text x=\"168.3\" y=\"218.5\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">kommen</text><line x1=\"228.1\" y1=\"212.0\" x2=\"294.0\" y2=\"212.0\" class=\"f-la\" marker-end=\"url(#imperative-acc)\"/><rect x=\"306.0\" y=\"192.0\" width=\"97.8\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-boxa\"/><text x=\"354.9\" y=\"218.5\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-a\" font-weight=\"700\">Kommen</text><rect x=\"409.8\" y=\"192.0\" width=\"56.6\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-box\"/><text x=\"438.2\" y=\"218.5\" font-size=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">Sie!</text><text x=\"480.5\" y=\"217.0\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"start\" class=\"f-m\">순서만 바꿔요</text><text x=\"300.0\" y=\"254.0\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-t\" font-weight=\"700\">동사가 맨 앞에 오고, 끝에 느낌표를 써요</text></svg></div><figcaption>명령형은 현재형에서 만들어요</figcaption></figure><p>명령형은 동사가 문장 맨 앞에 오고, 문장 끝에 느낌표를 써요. 누구에게 말하느냐에 따라 모양이 셋이에요.</p><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left t-first\"><thead><tr><th>상대</th><th>만드는 법</th><th>예</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>du</td><td>어간만 (주어 없음)</td><td>Komm! · Lern! · Mach!</td></tr><tr><td>ihr</td><td>ihr 형태 그대로 (주어 없음)</td><td>Kommt! · Lernt! · Macht!</td></tr><tr><td>Sie</td><td>원형 + Sie</td><td>Kommen Sie! · Lernen Sie!</td></tr><tr><td>wir (권유)</td><td>원형 + wir</td><td>Gehen wir!<span class=\"tc-ko\">가자!</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>du 명령형의 세부 규칙</h3><div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"t-left\"><thead><tr><th>동사 유형</th><th>du 명령형</th><th>예</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>규칙 동사</td><td>어간</td><td>mach<strong>en</strong> → Mach! · kauf<strong>en</strong> → Kauf!</td></tr><tr><td>어간 -t·-d·-ig</td><td>어간 + e</td><td>Arbeite! · Warte! · Entschuldige!</td></tr><tr><td>e → i / ie 동사</td><td>바뀐 모음 그대로, -st만 빼요</td><td>Sprich! · Nimm! · Iss! · Lies! · Hilf! · Gib!</td></tr><tr><td>a → ä 동사</td><td>움라우트 없이 어간</td><td>Fahr! · Schlaf! · Lauf!</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"callout callout-warn\"><span class=\"co-badge co-warn\">sein과 haben의 명령형</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">sein: Sei ruhig! · Seid ruhig! · Seien Sie ruhig! — 조용히 해(요)!<br>haben: Hab Geduld! · Habt Geduld! · Haben Sie Geduld! — 참아(요)!</p></div></div><h3>명령을 부드럽게 하는 말</h3><p>bitte(부디·제발), mal(좀), doch(어서·좀)를 넣으면 말투가 부드러워져요.</p><div class=\"exl\"><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Komm <strong>doch</strong> mit!</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">같이 가자!</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Hilf mir <strong>mal</strong>!</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">나 좀 도와줘!</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Setzen Sie sich <strong>bitte</strong>!</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">앉으세요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Steh auf!</span><span class=\"exl-nt\">분리동사는 접두어가 끝으로 (11과)</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">일어나!</span></div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">명령형</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> (친구에게) '천천히 말해!' (sprechen)</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Sprichst langsam!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Sprech langsam!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) Sprich langsam!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Spricht langsam!</button></div><div class=\"qe\">e → i 동사는 바뀐 모음 그대로, -st만 빼요.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> (친구에게) '조심해서 운전해!' (fahren)</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Fahrt du vorsichtig!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Fähr vorsichtig!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Fährst vorsichtig!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) Fahr vorsichtig!</button></div><div class=\"qe\">a → ä 동사는 명령형에서 움라우트가 없어요.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> (선생님께) '천천히 말씀해 주세요.'</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Sprecht bitte langsam!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Sie sprechen bitte langsam!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) Sprechen Sie bitte langsam!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Sprich bitte langsam!</button></div><div class=\"qe\">Sie 명령형 → 원형 + Sie, 동사가 맨 앞.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> (아이들 여럿에게) '조용히 해!'</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Seien ruhig!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) Seid ruhig!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Sind ruhig!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Sei ruhig!</button></div><div class=\"qe\">ihr에게 → ihr 형태 seid.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> (친구에게) '잠깐 기다려!' (warten)</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) Warte mal!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Wartest mal!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Wartet du mal!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Wart mal!</button></div><div class=\"qe\">어간 -t → 어간 + e.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">6.</strong> (친구에게) '그 책 읽어!' (lesen)</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Liest das Buch!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Les das Buch!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Lese das Buch!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) Lies das Buch!</button></div><div class=\"qe\">e → ie 동사 → Lies!</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-H\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">H</span><h2>가장 많이 하는 실수</h2></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 1</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">du의 어미 -st를 -t로 써요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Du lernt Deutsch.<span class=\"tx-n\">er 형태</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Du lernst Deutsch.<span class=\"tx-n\">너는 독일어를 배워</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\">du는 -st, er와 ihr는 -t예요.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 2</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">어간 -t·-d에 -e-를 빼요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Er arbeit heute.<span class=\"tx-n\">어미 없음</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Er arbeitet heute.<span class=\"tx-n\">그는 오늘 일해요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\">-t·-d로 끝나는 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">어간<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">어간</span>동사원형에서 끝의 -en(-n)을 뗀 부분이에요. 여기에 인칭어미를 붙여요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen → lern-</span></span></span>은 du·er·ihr에서 -e-를 넣어요.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 3</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">ich에서도 모음을 바꿔요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich fähre nach Hause.<span class=\"tx-n\">ich에 움라우트</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich fahre nach Hause.<span class=\"tx-n\">나는 집에 가요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\">모음 변화는 du와 er·sie·es에서만 일어나요.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 4</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">명령형에 -st나 주어를 남겨요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Kommst! · Du komm!<span class=\"tx-n\">du 형태를 그대로</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Komm!<span class=\"tx-n\">와!</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\">du <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">명령형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">명령형</span>부탁·지시·권유를 할 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요. 동사가 문장 맨 앞에 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Komm! · Kommt! · Kommen Sie!</span></span></span>은 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">주어<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">주어</span>문장에서 동작이나 상태의 주인이에요. 독일어 주어는 1격이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Der Hund schläft. → der Hund</span></span></span> 없이 어간만 써요. Sie 명령형만 Sie를 남겨요.</div></div><div class=\"trap\"><div class=\"trap-head\"><span class=\"trap-badge\">실수 5</span><span class=\"trap-label\">Fehler</span></div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px\">wissen과 kennen을 섞어요</div><div class=\"trap-ex wrong\"><span style=\"color:var(--no);font-weight:700\">✕</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich weiß den Mann.<span class=\"tx-n\">사람에 wissen</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-ex right\"><span style=\"color:var(--ok);font-weight:700\">✓</span><span class=\"tx-b\">Ich kenne den Mann.<span class=\"tx-n\">나는 그 남자를 알아요</span></span></div><div class=\"trap-note\">사람·장소는 kennen, 사실·정보는 wissen이에요.</div></div><div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">바로 확인</span><span class=\"sub-title\">실수 피하기</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\"><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> 바른 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) Du arbeitest viel.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Du arbeitet viel.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Du arbeits viel.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Du arbeitst viel.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">어간 -t → du arbeitest.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> 바른 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Ich liest die Zeitung.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Ich lies die Zeitung.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) Ich lese die Zeitung.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Ich liese die Zeitung.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">ich는 모음이 바뀌지 않아요.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> (친구에게) '그거 먹어!'</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) Iss das!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Ess das!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Esst du das!</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Isst das!</button></div><div class=\"qe\">essen → du 명령형 Iss!</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> 바른 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Weiß du die Antwort?</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) Weißt du die Antwort?</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Wisst du die Antwort?</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Kennst du die Antwort?</button></div><div class=\"qe\">답(정보)을 안다 → wissen, du weißt.</div></div><div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> 바른 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Wir wohnst seit 2020 hier.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Wir haben seit 2020 hier gewohnt.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Wir wohnt seit 2020 hier.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) Wir wohnen seit 2020 hier.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">지금도 계속되는 일 → seit + 현재형, wir → -en.</div></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-I\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">I</span><h2>참고</h2></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">tun 하다</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">ich tue · du tust · er tut · wir tun · ihr tut · sie tun<br><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">원형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">원형</span>동사원형을 줄여 부르는 말이에요. 사전에 실린 동사의 기본 모양으로, 대부분 -en으로 끝나요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: lernen · gehen · arbeiten</span></span></span>이 -n으로만 끝나서 wir·sie도 tun이에요. Was tust du? 너 뭐 해?</p></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">동사의 자리</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">평서문에서 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">활용된 동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">활용된 동사</span>주어에 맞춰 끝을 바꾼 동사예요. 원형 lernen이 주어 ich를 만나면 lerne가 돼요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: ich lerne · du lernst · er lernt</span></span></span>는 언제나 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">두 번째 자리<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">두 번째 자리</span>평서문에서 주어에 맞춰 바꾼 동사가 서는 자리예요. 독일어 어순의 가장 중요한 규칙이에요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich lerne Deutsch. · Heute lerne ich Deutsch.</span></span></span>에 와요 — Heute <strong>lerne</strong> ich Deutsch.<br>어순은 6과에서 자세히 다뤄요.</p></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">mögen과 möchten</span><div><p style=\"margin:0 0 8px\">mögen(좋아하다)과 möchten(~⁠하고 싶다)은 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">화법조동사<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">화법조동사</span>능력·허락·의무·의지 같은 뜻을 더해 주는 동사예요. 본동사는 원형으로 문장 끝에 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: können · dürfen · müssen · sollen · wollen · mögen</span></span></span>처럼 변해요 — ich mag · du magst · er mag / ich möchte · du möchtest · er möchte.<br>10과에서 함께 정리해요.</p></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"sec-J\"><div class=\"sh\"><span class=\"sl\">J</span><h2>바로 쓰는 문장 · 일상 회화</h2></div><p><span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">현재형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">현재형</span>지금의 일, 습관, 가까운 미래를 말할 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Ich lerne Deutsch.</span></span></span>과 <span class=\"gt\" tabindex=\"0\">명령형<span class=\"gt-tip\"><span class=\"gt-t\">명령형</span>부탁·지시·권유를 할 때 쓰는 동사 형태예요. 동사가 문장 맨 앞에 와요.<span class=\"gt-ex\">예: Komm! · Kommt! · Kommen Sie!</span></span></span>으로 바로 말할 수 있는 문장이에요.</p><div class=\"exl talk-l\"><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Ich <strong>heiße</strong> Minsu.</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">이히 하이세 민수</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">제 이름은 민수예요.</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\">Was <strong>machst</strong> du am Wochenende?</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">바스 마흐스트 두 암 보헨엔데</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">주말에 뭐 해?</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\"><strong>Sprechen</strong> Sie Englisch?</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">슈프레헨 지 엥글리쉬</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">영어 하세요?</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\"><strong>Weißt</strong> du das?</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">바이스트 두 다스</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">너 그거 알아?</span></div><div class=\"exl-i\"><span class=\"exl-de\"><strong>Nimm</strong> doch noch ein Stück!</span><span class=\"talk-pr\">님 도흐 노흐 아인 슈튁</span><span class=\"exl-ko\">한 조각 더 먹어!</span></div></div></section>\n<section id=\"summary\"><div class=\"summary-card\"><h2 class=\"sum-title\">이 과 정리</h2><div><div class=\"sum-li\">현재형 = 어간 + 인칭어미 — ich -e · du -st · er -t · wir -en · ihr -t · sie/Sie -en</div><div class=\"sum-li\">어간 -t·-d(-chn·-ffn·-gn)는 du·er·ihr 앞에 -e- — du arbeitest · er arbeitet</div><div class=\"sum-li\">어간 -s·-ß·-z·-x는 du에 -t만 — du heißt · du tanzt</div><div class=\"sum-li\">-eln·-ern 동사는 wir·sie가 -n — wir sammeln, ich sammle</div><div class=\"sum-li\">e→i · e→ie · a→ä · au→äu는 du와 er에서만 — du sprichst · er fährt</div><div class=\"sum-li\">sein·haben·werden·wissen은 통째로 외워요 — bin·bist·ist / habe·hast·hat / werde·wirst·wird / weiß·weißt·weiß</div><div class=\"sum-li\">명령형 — du: Komm! · Sprich! · Fahr! / ihr: Kommt! / Sie: Kommen Sie! / sein: Sei · Seid · Seien Sie</div></div></div><div class=\"callout callout-note\" style=\"margin-top:20px\"><span class=\"co-badge co-note\">다음 ⏭ 6과</span><div>6과에서는 활용된 동사가 문장 어디에 서는지 배워요 — 평서문은 두 번째, 질문은 맨 앞.<br>의문사로 묻는 법과 문장 가운데 성분의 순서도 함께 정리해요.</div></div></section><section id=\"solutions\" class=\"solutions\"><h2 class=\"sol-title\">Lösungen — 정답 모아보기</h2><div class=\"sol-grid\"><div><b>2–4과 복습</b>1. mir · 2. Er · 3. einen · 4. die Autos</div><div><b>규칙 동사</b>1. wohnen · 2. lernst · 3. spielt · 4. trinkt · 5. komme · 6. hören</div><div><b>발음 때문에 바뀌는 동사</b>1. arbeitet · 2. heißt · 3. findest · 4. sammle · 5. wandern · 6. tanzt · 7. regnet</div><div><b>모음 변화 동사</b>1. spricht · 2. fährst · 3. Liest · 4. nehme · 5. nimmt · 6. esst · 7. schläft · 8. hält</div><div><b>sein · haben · werden · wissen</b>1. sind · 2. Habt · 3. wird · 4. Weißt · 5. kenne · 6. bist</div><div><b>명령형</b>1. Sprich langsam! · 2. Fahr vorsichtig! · 3. Sprechen Sie bitte langsam! · 4. Seid ruhig! · 5. Warte mal! · 6. Lies das Buch!</div><div><b>실수 피하기</b>1. Du arbeitest viel. · 2. Ich lese die Zeitung. · 3. Iss das! · 4. Weißt du die Antwort? · 5. Wir wohnen seit 2020 hier.</div></div></section>\n<div class=\"brand-foot\"><img src=\"%%A0%%\" alt=\"Sophia Deutsch Akademie\" class=\"foot-logo\"><div class=\"foot-name\">Sophia Deutsch Akademie</div><div class=\"foot-tag\">Innovative Learning Beyond the Traditional</div></div>\n"